WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.011 --> 00:00:01.844
- Doc!

00:00:04.002 --> 00:00:04.888
- Marty!

00:00:04.888 --> 00:00:07.024
- Wait, wait, wait, stop the movie.

00:00:07.024 --> 00:00:09.006
Why is this skateboarding, guitar playing,

00:00:09.006 --> 00:00:12.100
cute girl dating, 17 year old friends with

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.622
an AARP card carrying, plutonium stealing,

00:00:14.622 --> 00:00:17.539
flux capacitor creating,
crackpot scientist?

00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:19.278
Does no one else find it slightly odd

00:00:19.278 --> 00:00:22.279
that they're meeting in
an empty mall parking lot

00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:23.875
at 1:15 in the morning?

00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:25.899
I mean, this isn't your
normal high school friendship.

00:00:25.899 --> 00:00:29.013
They don't copy each
other's biology homework.

00:00:29.013 --> 00:00:31.387
They don't complain about girls.

00:00:31.387 --> 00:00:34.293
They don't go to movies on Friday nights.

00:00:34.293 --> 00:00:36.763
No, Marty McFly and Dr. Emmett Brown

00:00:36.763 --> 00:00:38.853
have more of a 'bros don't let bros

00:00:38.853 --> 00:00:40.965
'steal plutonium from Libyan Nationalists'

00:00:40.965 --> 00:00:42.390
kind of thing going on.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.756
- Doc, you don't just walk into a store

00:00:43.756 --> 00:00:45.691
and buy plutonium.

00:00:45.691 --> 00:00:47.310
- John Mulaney hilariously
pointed this out

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.496
in his Netflix special 'The Comeback Kid.'

00:00:49.496 --> 00:00:50.646
- Who's his best friend?

00:00:50.646 --> 00:00:52.171
A disgraced nuclear physicist.

00:00:52.171 --> 00:00:53.541
All right, proceed.

00:00:53.541 --> 00:00:56.888
- And he's right; it's
a little fucking weird.

00:00:56.888 --> 00:01:01.026
Not quite 'your mom having
the hots for you' weird,

00:01:01.026 --> 00:01:01.859
but just

00:01:03.657 --> 00:01:04.968
weird.

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:06.971
Bob Gale, the film's
co-writer and co-creator

00:01:06.971 --> 00:01:09.131
of the entire Back the Future universe,

00:01:09.131 --> 00:01:11.867
gave us his reason for
Doc and Marty's friendship

00:01:11.867 --> 00:01:13.354
back in 2011.

00:01:13.354 --> 00:01:15.850
"For years, Marty was told
that Doc Brown was dangerous,

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:17.570
"a crackpot, a lunatic.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.909
"So being a red-blooded
American teenage boy,

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:23.269
"age 13 or 14, he decided
to find out just why

00:01:23.269 --> 00:01:25.141
"this guy was so dangerous.

00:01:25.141 --> 00:01:27.192
"Marty snuck into Doc's
lab and was fascinated by

00:01:27.192 --> 00:01:28.344
"all the cool stuff that was there.

00:01:28.344 --> 00:01:29.688
"When Doc found him
there, he was delighted

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:31.259
"to find that Marty thought he was cool

00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:33.074
"and accepted him for what he was."

00:01:33.074 --> 00:01:34.657
13 or 14 years old?

00:01:35.568 --> 00:01:37.043
Bob, you made it weirder.

00:01:37.043 --> 00:01:39.096
First off, pick a year.

00:01:39.096 --> 00:01:41.138
Was he 13 or was he 14?

00:01:41.138 --> 00:01:42.456
This is your universe.

00:01:42.456 --> 00:01:44.723
There is no reason to be vague.

00:01:44.723 --> 00:01:47.267
And what cool stuff was
Marty fascinated by?

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:50.066
A room full of clocks,
an automated can opener,

00:01:50.066 --> 00:01:52.488
an overpowered speaker
that almost killed him?

00:01:52.488 --> 00:01:54.624
At face value, Marty seems
like a pretty cool kid.

00:01:54.624 --> 00:01:56.520
As I mentioned before, he's in a band.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.248
He can skateboard; he plays guitar,

00:01:58.248 --> 00:01:59.666
and he has an attractive girlfriend.

00:01:59.666 --> 00:02:01.826
But what other friends does Marty have?

00:02:01.826 --> 00:02:04.130
In fact, what friends does Marty make

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:06.757
over the course of three movies?

00:02:06.757 --> 00:02:09.323
We see him with his band,
but there doesn't seem

00:02:09.323 --> 00:02:11.134
to be any camaraderie amongst him and

00:02:11.134 --> 00:02:12.792
any of the other Pinheads.

00:02:12.792 --> 00:02:14.507
In the future, he still seems like a loner

00:02:14.507 --> 00:02:16.800
who's kind of stepped on
by all of his superiors.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.019
And in the wild west, his only friends

00:02:19.019 --> 00:02:23.186
are his ancestors who
suspiciously look a lot like him.

00:02:24.046 --> 00:02:25.486
And don't get me started on his incredibly

00:02:25.486 --> 00:02:26.795
depressing family life.

00:02:26.795 --> 00:02:27.659
His dad's a pushover,

00:02:27.659 --> 00:02:29.878
and his mom's an overbearing alcoholic.

00:02:29.878 --> 00:02:32.280
But what does Marty truly love?

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.648
Music.

00:02:33.648 --> 00:02:34.885
The franchise starts
with Marty getting blown

00:02:34.885 --> 00:02:36.504
away 30 feet by a speaker.

00:02:36.504 --> 00:02:38.690
He brainwashes his father
with heavy metal music,

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.450
and he lives his dream of performing

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.625
at the high school dance by
playing "Johnny B. Goode."

00:02:42.625 --> 00:02:44.520
When we first encounter
Doc Brown in the past

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.989
on November 5, 1955, you might not notice

00:02:47.989 --> 00:02:50.784
a saxophone hanging in the
background of his workshop.

00:02:50.784 --> 00:02:52.370
So let's say Bob Gale is right,

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.901
they met innocently early in the 1980's,

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:56.882
two loners who want so much more from life

00:02:56.882 --> 00:03:00.277
bond over their mutual love for music.

00:03:00.277 --> 00:03:01.538
One's stuck with a shitty home life

00:03:01.538 --> 00:03:02.807
trying to grasp his future.

00:03:02.807 --> 00:03:05.529
The other a disgraced scientist struggling

00:03:05.529 --> 00:03:07.523
with the constant failures of his past.

00:03:07.523 --> 00:03:09.096
It's innocent enough, but still

00:03:09.096 --> 00:03:12.014
something just doesn't quite add up.

00:03:12.014 --> 00:03:13.778
Which brings me to my next theory:

00:03:13.778 --> 00:03:16.560
what else do slacker teenagers love?

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.393
Sleep.

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:20.846
Marty is constantly sleeping or passed out

00:03:20.846 --> 00:03:23.368
or knocked unconscious over
the course of the trilogy,

00:03:23.368 --> 00:03:25.976
and every time he wakes
up, he's very confused

00:03:25.976 --> 00:03:27.147
and disoriented.

00:03:27.147 --> 00:03:30.482
But like most slackers, Marty
is a kid with big dreams:

00:03:30.482 --> 00:03:32.414
getting signed by the record company,

00:03:32.414 --> 00:03:33.902
taking Jennifer up to the lake,

00:03:33.902 --> 00:03:35.485
and maybe, possibly

00:03:37.908 --> 00:03:40.260
of time traveling with
an imaginary best friend

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.398
who can fix all the problems in his life.

00:03:42.398 --> 00:03:46.078
Maybe Marty McFly is a lucid dreamer.

00:03:46.078 --> 00:03:47.364
- It's all a dream.

00:03:47.364 --> 00:03:50.257
It's just a very intense dream.

00:03:50.257 --> 00:03:52.212
- And he dreams up the
time traveling DeLorean.

00:03:52.212 --> 00:03:53.486
And he dreams up the...

00:03:53.486 --> 00:03:55.092
- Good, kind and loyal friend.

00:03:55.092 --> 00:03:57.709
- And it makes sense 'cause
he's in desperate need of one.

00:03:57.709 --> 00:04:01.630
Someone or something to
make the pain go away.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.538
His Oedipus complex with
his mom...subconscious.

00:04:04.538 --> 00:04:06.074
His triumphant strut across

00:04:06.074 --> 00:04:08.846
the Hill Valley High
School auditorium stage...

00:04:08.846 --> 00:04:11.281
pure aspirational imagination.

00:04:11.281 --> 00:04:14.858
- If you put your mind to it,
you can accomplish anything.

00:04:14.858 --> 00:04:17.870
- How else do you explain
Mr. Strickland never aging?

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:21.073
Well, it's either that or Marty met Doc

00:04:21.073 --> 00:04:23.341
innocently as writer Bob Gale said around

00:04:23.341 --> 00:04:25.790
the age of 13 or 14, and
he's been hanging around

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.922
Doc's workshop for three to four years

00:04:27.922 --> 00:04:30.816
and somehow never noticed or heard Doc

00:04:30.816 --> 00:04:34.788
talk about his 30 year mission
of building a time machine.

00:04:34.788 --> 00:04:36.302
Are you kidding me?

00:04:36.302 --> 00:04:38.522
In all of this time around his best bud,

00:04:38.522 --> 00:04:41.450
Marty never heard one
mention of the infamous

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.322
flux capacitor?

00:04:43.322 --> 00:04:45.278
Never once saw a DeLorean?

00:04:45.278 --> 00:04:47.114
Are we really supposed to believe that

00:04:47.114 --> 00:04:49.044
the inquisitive Marty McFly never asked

00:04:49.044 --> 00:04:51.010
Doc what he was working on?

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:53.521
Or that Doc Brown wouldn't
tell his only friend

00:04:53.521 --> 00:04:56.353
that he invented time travel?

00:04:56.353 --> 00:04:57.530
I call bullshit.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:01.130
Marty McFly is asleep, dreaming of sweet

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.530
Huey Lewis and the News
tunes, time traveling

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:07.025
in a dope DeLorean with his
kooky best friend, Doc Brown,

00:05:07.025 --> 00:05:09.686
fixing the past in an
attempt to make his actual

00:05:09.686 --> 00:05:13.874
real life lonely present
slightly more tolerable.

00:05:13.874 --> 00:05:14.991
Too dark?

00:05:14.991 --> 00:05:16.202
Okay.

00:05:16.202 --> 00:05:17.844
Well, let me go back and
touch on that whole thing

00:05:17.844 --> 00:05:20.369
with Marty and his mom for one second...

00:05:20.369 --> 00:05:22.702
(explosion)

00:05:27.164 --> 00:05:29.747
(upbeat music)

